now moved into the translation of repairing the world that that was not the original understanding of that phrase the original our understanding of that phrase really had to do and I'm willing to be corrected on this But my understanding of it is it really had to do with getting rid of idolatry idolatry idols and But, you know, for the vast majority of those who identify as Jewish Americans or American Jews, Steve, the vast majority are not that religious. The Orthodox community is not the majoritarian movement in the Jewish community in America. And yet the Orthodox community, which you might say is the one that followed the Bible or the Torah, the most closely or the most with the most with the most with the most seriousness. Guess what? They tend to vote Republican. Isn't that interesting?",
